title: DevShell Environment Prototype Tasks
status: implemented
created: 2026-11-07
author: adrian
items[8]{id,title,description,criteria,complexity,effort,dependencies,refs}:
  T-001,[x] "Scaffold the harness crate","Create adrs/2026-11-07-devshell-environment/poc/prepare with its own Cargo.toml (serde, serde_json, toml) and a binary that takes a declared step. It is not a workspace member: the root Cargo.toml already excludes adrs, and nothing in crates/ may refer to it.","cargo build inside poc/prepare succeeds; the workspace's cargo metadata does not list the crate; no path dependency from any crate points at it.",low,"1-2h",,"prototype-not-shipped,no-new-dependency"
  T-002,[x] "Model the step and its contributions","Step { identity, kind, settings } with the kind parsed as a string, Requirement { scope, name }, Contributions { environment, mounts }. Settings are typed per kind by the harness so an unknown key or a missing installable fails at parse rather than at launch.","A devshell step with an installable parses; an unknown key and a missing installable each fail naming the key; both are tests. The harness branches on the kind in exactly one place, and the number of branches is written down for the findings.",low,"1-2h",T-001,"two-kinds,contributions,requirements,step-shape-refused"
  T-003,[x] "Check the host before doing any work","nix on PATH with its version, flakes enabled, the installable evaluates, and path-info reports the devShell valid. Each check returns a structured result with a reason and a remedy, and a failure exits before print-dev-env runs.","With a PATH lacking nix the harness exits non-zero naming nix and a remedy; with an unbuilt derivation it reports not valid and writes only the .drv; a failed check adds no store path; each check has a test.",medium,"2-4h",T-002,"host-readiness,no-realisation,no-nix-refused,unrealised-refused,flakes-disabled,legible-unavailability"
  T-004,[x] "Prepare the environment","print-dev-env --json for the baseline and the output path, then the devShell entered under env -i with only HOME and a minimal PATH, writing NUL-separated records to a file. Values come from the entered environment; provenance is the names that differ from the baseline. Shell state and backend-supplied values are dropped.","The variable count is within a small delta of T-011's 91; RUSTFLAGS carries no caller data; SSH_AUTH_SOCK, DOCKER_HOST, DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS and WAYLAND_DISPLAY are absent; a banner-printing hook does not corrupt the records; a failing hook is reported with bounded output; a hook that execs another shell is recorded as the risk it is.",medium,"3-5h",T-003,"environment,environment-is-devshells,no-shell-state,no-values-on-surfaces,hook-fails,hook-prints,hook-execs-shell"
  T-005,[x] "Turn the closure into mounts","path-info -r over the output path, de-duplicated and absolute, one read-only mount per path. A store-view switch selects the whole store instead. Record the count, the query and setup time, and the bwrap argv size.","The mount list equals the de-duplicated query output; the count matches T-022's 238 for this flake; the whole-store switch yields one mount; the argv size is recorded and the launch succeeds with it.",low,"1-2h",T-004,"store-closure,closure-equals-query,backend-cannot-mount"
  T-006,[x] "Launch the workload with the contributions","Feed lbx-bwrap the mounts as reads, the prepared environment and cargo test -p agentkit-path. The sandbox has no network and a read-only store.","cargo test -p agentkit-path passes inside the sandbox; the sandbox has no route to the host network; /nix/store is read-only; the launcher's environment is exactly the prepared one, with no caller variable added.",medium,"2-4h","T-004,T-005","contributions,contributions-at-position,no-socket-or-network,no-nix-inside,host-placement"
  T-007,[x] "Refuse a missing requirement","Declare a sandbox requirement the view cannot meet, such as a path that is not mounted or a shell the sandbox lacks, and show that the refusal is structured and happens before anything is launched.","The refusal names the requirement, its scope, the reason and the remedy; no sandbox process starts; the same step with the requirement satisfied proceeds. One test per scope.",low,"1-2h",T-005,"requirements,requirement-refused,fail-closed,failure-classes"
  T-008,[x] "Write the findings","Record the answers beside the crate: Q1 whether a kind the contract does not name survives a real launcher and what moving ProvisionKind and ProvisionStep to identity plus kind plus settings would cost; Q2 what a backend must report. Include the measurements and everything refuted, including the dirty-tree source write, the path-info refusal and the absence of shell state.","Each question has an answer with the command that produced it and an output excerpt; every measurement in the plan is present and reproducible from the file; the decisions left to the follow-up are listed; no claim appears without a citation.",low,"1-2h","T-006,T-007","boundary-proven,prototype-not-shipped,documentation"
